# G062 — Chart Maker

*v2. See `chart-maker.md` for prose: scale abstraction (linear/ordinal),
chart type as closed enum, backend-agnostic rendering (ascii/svg/html).*

---

## Choreographic Case: Weekly Dashboard

[weekly-dashboard
    IN ORDER TO
        render a weekly revenue bar chart and pace-score line chart
        into a single ascii-art report
        that the resolver can later re-render as SVG or HTML

    @revenue <- [sql[query {statement: "select day, sum(amount) from orders where week = @this-week group by day"}]]
    @pace-scores <- [daily-notes[map {field: "pace_score"}]]

    @bar <- [chart[bar-chart {title: "Weekly Revenue",
                                data: @revenue,
                                encode: {x: "day", y: "total"}}]]
    @line <- [chart[line-chart {title: "Pace Score Trend",
                                  data: @pace-scores,
                                  encode: {x: "day", y: "score"}}]]

    @report <- [chart[render-all {charts: [@bar, @line],
                                    backend: "ascii"}]]

    @report
        where
            backend is in ["ascii", "svg", "html"]
            and every chart has at least one data point
            and render produced non-empty output
        || -> #render-failed @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[scale
    linear          {domain-min, domain-max, range-min, range-max}
    linear-at       {scale, x}
    linear-fit      {values, range-min, range-max, include-zero?}
    ordinal         {categories, range-min, range-max}
]

[chart
    bar-chart       {title, data, encode, width?}
    line-chart      {title, data, encode, width?, height?}
    scatter-chart   {title, data, encode}
    histogram       {title, values, bins?}
    render          {chart, backend?}
    render-all      {charts, backend?}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: backend as bare-word string, not enum

The v1 modeled backend as `enum Backend { Ascii, Svg, Html }`. In
Innate the backend is a bare-word string; the resolver picks the
rendering path:

[chart[render {chart: @c, backend: "ascii"}
    where
        "ascii" renders to a text-mode box-drawing grid
        and "svg" renders to SVG markup
        and "html" wraps SVG in an html table
]

Adding a new backend is a resolver extension — no grammar change.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @data <- [{day: "Mon", total: 120}
               {day: "Tue", total: 85}
               {day: "Wed", total: 210}
               {day: "Thu", total: 180}
               {day: "Fri", total: 95}]

    @bar <- [chart[bar-chart {title: "Weekly Revenue",
                                data: @data,
                                encode: {x: "day", y: "total"}}]]
    -> [chart[render {chart: @bar, backend: "ascii"}]]
    ;; -> 5-bar ASCII chart with labeled axes

    @scale <- [scale[linear-fit {values: [120, 85, 210, 180, 95],
                                   range-min: 0, range-max: 20,
                                   include-zero?: true}]]
    -> [scale[linear-at {scale: @scale, x: 210}]]   ;; -> 20 (max maps to range-max)
]
